Neverball (apps/neverball)

Game and engine (engine/)
  Neverball, by Robert Kooima and the Neverball contributors (doc/authors.txt
  in the source).
  License: GNU General Public License, version 2 or later (engine/COPYING).
  Source: https://github.com/Neverball/neverball, commit
  2821e1e47de84cc9a743277dcd4152be3766a374, with frunk.store's changes for this
  site in engine/neverball-web.patch (also tools/neverball/neverball-web.patch
  in https://github.com/RobertPKyle/frunk-store, whose
  tools/build-neverball.mjs builds it). The source the build came from, with
  the levels' map files, is engine/neverball-2821e1e47de8-web-src.tar.gz.
  The changes: the project's package downloads off, since all the level sets
  come with the game; the browser's standard controller layout; every
  controller press counts, since the page shows the game only the pads it
  should read; no pause when the frame loses focus and no controller loss
  either, since the page pauses when it's really hidden; no Exit or
  switch-to-Neverputt button; a screen-change counter for the page's
  end-to-end check. Neverputt's courses (they are their own app on this site),
  the Octocat ball (used with GitHub's permission to the Neverball project)
  and the Chinese and Korean font are left out. The page's Picture setting
  chooses the drawing resolution.
  The engine includes gl4es (MIT, https://github.com/ptitSeb/gl4es, commit
  c9895df34cd466c23bc60c2bd3db3d87e98fcbe7), miniz (MIT) and Emscripten's SDL2,
  SDL2_ttf, FreeType, libpng and libjpeg ports under their own licenses (see
  doc/legal in the source). The game's font is DejaVu Sans Bold (see
  doc/legal/license-DejaVu.txt).

Game data (engine/neverball.data, preloaded at /data)
  The eight level sets, balls, textures, sounds and music as the Neverball
  project publishes them, under the project's license (LICENSE.md in the
  source).

Page
  audio.js is from Neverball's js/index.html, under the same license.
  index.html, neverball.js and icon.svg: by frunk.store.
